+# CVE-2026-22185 -- False Positive Analysis for openldap (Debian 12 Bookworm)
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## Executive Summary
+
+CVE-2026-22185 describes a heap buffer underflow in the `mdb_load`
+utility of LMDB (Lightning Memory-Mapped Database).
+
+Although scanners frequently associate this CVE with the `openldap`
+package, the vulnerable utility (`mdb_load`) is **not built, not
+shipped, and not reachable** in Debian 12 (Bookworm)'s `openldap` binary
+packages.
+
+Therefore, this CVE is classified as a:
+
+**False Positive for openldap on Debian 12 (Bookworm)**
+
+Remediation applies only to the `lmdb` / `lmdb-utils` package.
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## CVE Details
+
+  Field               Value
+  ------------------- -------------------------------------------
+  CVE ID              CVE-2026-22185
+  Component           LMDB -- `mdb_load` utility
+  CWE                 CWE-125 (Out-of-bounds Read)
+  Affected Versions   LMDB ≤ 0.9.14 (prior to commit 8e1fda8)
+  Fixed Commit        8e1fda85532a3c74276df38a42d234dcdfa1e40d
+  Impact              Limited denial of service (utility crash)
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## Debian 12 (Bookworm) Package Versions
+
+openldap: 2.5.13+dfsg-5\
+lmdb: 0.9.24-1
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## Why This Is a False Positive for openldap
+
+### 1. openldap Does Not Ship `mdb_load`
+
+Binary packages built from openldap:
+
+-   slapd
+-   ldap-utils
+-   libldap-2.5-0
+-   libldap-common
+-   libldap-dev
+-   libldap2-dev
+-   slapd-contrib
+-   slapd-smbk5pwd
+-   slapi-dev
+
+Installed ldap-utils binaries:
+
+/usr/bin/ldapadd\
+/usr/bin/ldapcompare\
+/usr/bin/ldapdelete\
+/usr/bin/ldapexop\
+/usr/bin/ldapmodify\
+/usr/bin/ldapmodrdn\
+/usr/bin/ldappasswd\
+/usr/bin/ldapsearch\
+/usr/bin/ldapurl\
+/usr/bin/ldapwhoami
+
+`mdb_load` is NOT installed by openldap.
+
+It is shipped only by:
+
+lmdb-utils
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+### 2. LMDB Source Exists but Is Not Built
+
+The openldap source contains:
+
+libraries/liblmdb/mdb_load.c
+
+However, `liblmdb` is not included in the build system SUBDIRS:
+
+SUBDIRS = liblutil liblber liblunicode libldap librewrite
+
+Therefore:
+
+-   Not compiled
+-   Not installed
+-   Not reachable
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+### 3. Where the CVE Actually Applies
+
+In Debian 12:
+
+-   `mdb_load` is built from the `lmdb` source package
+-   Shipped in `lmdb-utils`
+
+CVE-2026-22185 applies to:
+
+lmdb\
+lmdb-utils
+
+It does NOT apply to openldap.
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## Runtime Verification
+
+dpkg -L openldap \| grep mdb_load\
+\# no output
+
+dpkg -L ldap-utils \| grep mdb_load\
+\# no output
+
+dpkg -L lmdb-utils \| grep mdb_load\
+\# /usr/bin/mdb_load
+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+## Final Conclusion
+
+CVE-2026-22185 affects only the standalone `mdb_load` utility.
+
+Debian 12 openldap:
+
+-   Does not build it
+-   Does not ship it
+-   Does not expose it
+
+Therefore:
+
+CVE-2026-22185 is not exploitable via any binary shipped by openldap in
+Debian 12 (Bookworm) and is classified as a False Positive for this
+package.
+
+Remediation belongs exclusively to the lmdb package.
