Description: CVE-2020-15719 - Change TLS_REQSAN default from allow to try
 When a TLS certificate contains SubjectAltName (SAN) entries that
 don't match the hostname, OpenLDAP should not fall back to checking
 the Common Name (CN). This prevents potential MITM attacks per RFC6125.
 .
 OpenLDAP 2.5.x already includes the TLS_REQSAN infrastructure (from
 ITS#9318) which allows configuring SAN checking behavior. However, the
 default is "allow" which still permits CN fallback when SANs are present
 but don't match. This patch changes the default to "try" so that when
 SANs are present but none match, the connection is rejected instead of
 falling back to CN checking.
